<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Birger Jarl</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1210–<a href="/years/1266">1266</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Birger Magnusson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Birger Jarl was a Swedish statesman who held the office of jarl from 1248 and governed for his son King Valdemar, founding the Folkung dynasty. He strengthened royal law and authority, is traditionally credited with founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholm</a> around 1250, and led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> that brought Tavastia in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> under Swedish rule in the mid-13th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/birger-jarl.jpg" alt="Birger Jarl" width="255" height="353" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Axel Forssén (1888-1961) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Birger_jarl_(Forss%C3%A9n).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
